🎯 Real World Scenario where radis cache use ?
Library me:
        - 📖 Books = Database data
        - 👨‍🎓 Students = Users / Clients
        - 🧑‍💼 Store Keeper = Application Server (Spring Boot)
        - 🗄️ Main Racks = Database (MySQL, PostgreSQL etc.)
        - 🧺 Counter pe rakhi popular books = Redis Cache
🏗️ Without Cache (Direct Database Access) :
🔁 Kya ho raha hai?
        - Student bolta hai: "Mujhe Harry Potter chahiye"
        - Store keeper jaata hai rack pe
        - Book dhundta hai
        - Student ko deta hai
        - Next student fir wahi book maangta hai
        - Store keeper fir rack pe jaata hai
👉 Har baar rack check karna = Har baar database hit karna
❌ Problem :
        - Rack door hai → Time lagta hai
        - Agar 100 students Harry Potter maang rahe hain → 100 baar rack check
        - Database slow ho sakta hai
        - Load increase hoga
⚡ With Redis Cache :
           - Ab smart store keeper kya karta hai?
           - Pehle student ne Harry Potter maangi
           - Store keeper rack (Database) se book laaya
           - Ek copy counter pe rakh di (Redis Cache)
           - Ab jo bhi student aayega:
                                - Pehle counter check hoga
                                - Wahi se book de di jayegi
                                - Rack tak jaane ki zarurat nahi

Note:-
In modern projects, Redis is integrated using:
  - Spring Boot
  - Spring Cache abstraction
  - @Cacheable, @CachePut, @CacheEvict
Example:
@Cacheable("users")
public User getUser(Long id) {
    return userRepository.findById(id).get();
}
👉 Spring handles caching
👉 Redis stores the data

 What is cache ?
Cache is a temporary storage that keeps frequently used data so it can be accessed faster instead of fetching it again from the database or API.

Why use caching ?
- Reduce latency : faster access to data compared to fetching from a database or an external service.
- Decrease Load : Reduces the number of calls to the backend system or database.
- improve scalability : helps applications handle higher traffic loads efficiently.

How many Types of Cache ?
1️⃣ Location Based Types of Cache.
  1. In-Memory
  2. Distributed

1. In-Memory :
   - Data, application ke memory (RAM) me store hota hai.
   - store krne ke liye used krta hai :
                                 - Java ConcurrentMap.
                                 - Caffeine
                                 - EhCache
   - Server restart pe data chala jaata hai.
   - Sirf ek application instance ke liye kaam karta hai.
   - Very fast (no network call)
🧠 In-Memory Cache Limitation :
  - Suppose tumne 3 instances deploy kiye:
                             ┌───────────────┐
             Client ───────► │  Instance 1  │
                             └───────────────┘
                             ┌───────────────┐
             Client ───────► │  Instance 2  │
                             └───────────────┘
                             ┌───────────────┐
             Client ───────► │  Instance 3  │
                             └───────────────┘
       ⚠️ Har instance ka apna separate RAM hoga.
   ❌ Problem 1: Data Inconsistency :
         Example:
              - User request Pune weather
              - Load balancer request Instance 1 pe bhejta hai
              - Instance 1 cache me store karta hai
         Next request:
              - Load balancer request Instance 2 pe bhej deta hai
              - Instance 2 ke cache me data nahi
              - Fir DB hit karega ❌
             👉 Caching ka fayda kam ho gaya
   ❌ Problem 2: Update Issue
              - Suppose weather update hua:
              - Instance 1 ne cache update kiya
              - Instance 2 & 3 ke cache me purana data abhi bhi hai
              👉 Stale data problem 😵

2. Distributed Cache :
     - Multiple servers ke beech shared cache.
     - store krne ke liye use krta hai:
                                  - Redis.
                                  - Memcached
     - Scalable hota hai.
     - Multiple application instances same cache use kar sakti hain.
     - Load balancing friendly.
     - Suitable for microservices.
     - Centralized caching.

🔥 Annotations Used in Caching ?
@EnableCaching :
           - Caching feature ko activate karta hai.
           - Main class pe (generally Spring Boot Application class pe).
           - or configuration class bna ke use kr skte is annotation ko.
@Cacheable :
          - Pehle cache check karta hai.
          - Agar data mil gaya → method execute nahi hoga.
          - Agar nahi mila → method execute hoga → result cache me store hoga.
          - Mostly Use: Read operations (GET APIs).
          - Example:
          @Cacheable(value = "weatherCache", key = "#city")
          public String getWeatherByCity(String city) {
              return weatherRepository.findByCity(city)
                      .map(Weather::getForecast)
                      .orElse("Not Found");
          }
          Note:
             - value = cache ka name
             - key = Cache ke andar data kis naam se store hoga.
@CachePut :
          - Method hamesha execute hoga.
          - Result cache me update karega.
          - Mostly update operation me use hota hai.
          - Example:
                   @CachePut(value = "weatherCache", key = "#weather.city")
                   public String updateWeather(Weather weather) {
                       weatherRepository.save(weather);
                       return weather.getForecast();
                   }
@CacheEvict :
          - Cache se data remove karta hai.
          - Mostly delete operation me use hota hai.
          - Example:
                 @CacheEvict(value = "weatherCache", key = "#city")
                 public void deleteWeather(String city) {
                     weatherRepository.deleteByCity(city);
                 }
          - Sab cache clear karna ho:  @CacheEvict(value = "weatherCache", allEntries = true)

@Caching :
        - Multiple caching annotations ek sath use karne ke liye.
        - Example:
            @Caching(
                put = {
                    @CachePut(value = "weatherCache", key = "#weather.city")
                },
                evict = {
                    @CacheEvict(value = "otherCache", allEntries = true)
                }
            )
Note:- @Cacheable skips method execution if data exists in cache,
       while @CachePut always executes the method and updates cache.


🔥 What is Redis Cache?
   - Redis ek in-memory data store hai jo data ko RAM me store karta hai taaki application ko fast response mile.
   - Jab hum Redis ko caching ke liye use karte hain, to use kehte hain Redis Cache.

🔥 Connect Spring boot App to Redis :
  STEP-1 :
      - Installed docker on AWS.
      - ensure docker up and running
  STEP-2 :
      - Agar Docker installed hai, to bas ye command chala do: docker run --name <redis-cachename> -p 6379:6379 -d redis
      - Redis CLI open karne ke liye: docker exec -it redis redis-cli
      - Test: ping
      - Output aayega: PONG
     👉 Matlab Redis chal raha hai ✅
  STEP-3 :
       - application.properties me:
                           spring.cache.type=redis
                           spring.data.redis.host= localhost / <EC2-public-IP>
                           spring.data.redis.port=6379
       - Dependency:
                 <dependency>
                     <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                     <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-redis</artifactId>
                 </dependency>


Note:- to see data use redis cli like,

redis-cli  -> press enter
               get weather::Pune
               keys *




